# Patch-ID: P-TAB-001 (slice S3) — typed tab/navigation event surface + observer
# Area: tab.
# Rationale: rearc.ipc.v1 §§3-4 require an E->S event vocabulary (tab.created /
#   tab.updated / tab.closed / navigation.committed / navigation.failed) before
#   any transport exists. S3 ships the typed C++ surface and the per-session
#   WebContentsObserver that produces it; the wire envelope (message_id,
#   correlation, serialization, in-process typed side channel) arrives with the
#   transport slice. Day-one scaffolding: events go to a registered
#   TabEventSink; with no sink they drop with a VLOG — the same pattern as
#   app/005's readiness sink and tab/006's native-window provider seam.
# Additive only. Files:
#   - ipc_tab_events.{h,cc} — TabEvent struct (sparse has_* change fields per
#     §3 tab.updated; navigation fields per §4), TabEventKindName() returning
#     the wire-name literals ("tab.created" etc. — the slice-plan §6 strings
#     gate keys on them), TabEventSink registration, generation-stamped
#     EmitTabEvent (unknown/destroyed sessions drop EXCEPT kTabClosed, which
#     races session teardown and carries the caller's last-known generation),
#     EmitTabCreatedEvent / EmitInitialSnapshotEvent (§3: tab.created first,
#     then a fully-populated tab.updated baseline).
#   - tab_observer.{h,cc} — one TabObserver per session, attached via
#     AttachTabObserver only after tab.created (§3 ordering). navigation.* is
#     filtered to IsInPrimaryMainFrame(); committed vs failed splits on
#     HasCommitted(); ERR_ABORTED still emits navigation.failed (it is a
#     cancellation, not a silent drop). navigation_id maps the session-stable
#     bridge ID from NavigationHandle::GetNavigationId() — never a raw
#     pointer, the handle is never retained (§4). A renderer crash emits
#     is_crashed=true and is NOT a close (§3). WebContentsDestroyed emits
#     tab.closed (final event) and self-detaches via a POSTED task — no
#     destruction inside a content callback.
# No call sites are wired in this slice: AttachTabObserver /
# EmitTabCreatedEvent are integration seams invoked by the (later) IPC layer
# wiring, because TabRegistry::CreateSession lives in tab/007's frozen file.
# Hunk placement: the BUILD.gn sources block sits between
# "file_select_helper_mac.mm" and "fullscreen_mac.mm" — its -U3 context
# overlaps tab/007's after-context only on lines neither patch changes
# (series-mechanics: context-only overlap is permitted).
